 ## Overview
-This family defines the static data structures and topological resolution strategies required to map the 256 binary configurations of a voxel's corner signs to specific isosurface triangulations. It solves the problem of determining edge intersections and triangle connectivity without runtime branching logic for topology [Lookup Table and Ambiguity Handling](10327-lookup-table-and-ambiguity-handling.md). The standard lookup tables provide O(1) topology determination but fail to guarantee manifold connectivity for 8 specific "ambiguous" cases where the isosurface passes through the cube center [Lookup Table and Ambiguity Handling](10327-lookup-table-and-ambiguity-handling.md). This family encompasses the definition of these tables, methods for resolving the resulting topological inconsistencies (cracks/holes), and variants that modify the table or classification logic to handle edge cases like exact ties or multi-material interfaces.
