 ### [Marching Cubes Iso-surface Extraction](6921-marching-cubes-iso-surface-extraction.md)
-Marching Cubes is a polygonization algorithm that extracts a triangular mesh representing an isosurface from 3D scalar volumetric data by identifying where the scalar field crosses a specific threshold value. It builds on [Lookup Table and Ambiguity Handling](10327-lookup-table-and-ambiguity-handling.md) by applying the precomputed `edgeTable` and `triangleTable` to every voxel in the volume to generate a continuous manifold. Unlike direct volume rendering which displays all data via ray casting, this method isolates specific structures (e.g., bone or tissue) by thresholding, resulting in a lightweight polygonal mesh suitable for interactive rotation and lighting.
