 ### [Marching Cubes Isosurface Tie-Breaking](10380-marching-cubes-isosurface-tie-breaking.md)
-This method resolves topological inconsistencies in the Marching Cubes algorithm that arise when the isosurface value exactly equals a voxel's scalar value. It ensures that adjacent voxels sharing a face classify that face identically, preventing mesh holes caused by incompatible triangulations. It differs from general ambiguity handling (e.g., [Topology and Ambiguity Handling](6547-topology-and-ambiguity-handling.md)) by focusing specifically on the deterministic resolution of exact ties rather than saddle-point topology correction [G].
