 ### [Marching Cubes for EB Generation](14133-marching-cubes-for-eb-generation.md)
-This method generates Embedded Boundary (EB) geometry on 3D Cartesian grids by resolving a surface using the Marching Cubes 33 (MC33) lookup tables, computing volume/area fractions, centroids, normals, and connectivity. It improves upon the legacy EB generation method by providing a more accurate single-valued representation of the boundary. It is distinguished from standard isosurface extraction by its integration into the AMReX EB framework, specifically handling exact edge intersections via root finding or STL intersection, caching these intersections in `MCFab` structures for downstream aperture construction, and enforcing single-valued topological constraints.
