 ### [Rule-based Marching Method](14180-rule-based-marching-method.md)
-The rule-based marching method is a topology generation technique for volume fraction data that derives partial vertex labeling and uses lookup tables to determine material interface configurations in mixed cells. Unlike methods that force vertex labels via volume averaging or cast data onto dual meshes, this approach implies labels through a small set of logical rules, leaving topology uninitialized when the labeling is ambiguous or insufficient. It is specifically designed to handle multiple materials and complex features like thin filaments by allowing multiple intersections per edge, which standard binary marching cubes do not support.
